VibeDev i18n — third-party translation attribution
===================================================

The base Simplified-Chinese translation data in this directory
(`zh-CN.json`) and the do-not-translate ruleset (`do_not_translate.json`),
together with the `zedl10n` build-time replacement tool used by `build-zh.ps1`,
are derived from:

    zed-globalization  —  https://github.com/x6nux/zed-globalization
    (a localization fork of the Zed editor)

zed-globalization is licensed under GPL-3.0 — the same license as Zed and as
this VibeDev fork (GPL-3.0-or-later) — so its translation data is reused here
under those terms. All credit for the Chinese translations of upstream Zed
strings goes to the zed-globalization project and its contributors.

`vibedev-overrides.json` contains VibeDev-specific strings translated by the
VibeDev project. The "VibeDev" product name itself is left untranslated.

The base `zh-CN.json` corresponds to zed-globalization's `v1.4.2-pre` snapshot.
Refresh it from their `i18n` branch when rebasing onto a newer upstream Zed.
